at_resets_an_ignored_sigtrap_stops_the_run`, `a_thread_that_blocks_sigtrap_never_arms_and_the_trace_says_so`, `a_watch_survives_exec_into_an_image_that_stores_first`, `an_access_trace_leaves_a_replayed_run_unchanged`, `watch_hits_name_both_writers_and_leave_the_run_unchanged` passed. Main has since moved to `e4eda3b4b`; this head merges into it without a code conflict (pin files only, left to the lander). Revision 5 was `01f999643`.\n\n**Revision 7:** rebased onto main `cd9e333e8`, on #4739's new head `2b76d7f60` (Reverie pin unchanged). Code conflicts resolved: Moved onto #4739's head on main cd9e333e8 with this change's own lines unchanged apart from its RPC row: in detcore-model config.rs the legacy-key list is the union, 48 long with K=33, `watch` and `watch_from` following main's new `standard_stream_aliases` (34a4c267c) in the list and the count comment, with assert keys.len() + 33; main took global RPC revision 20 (34a4c267c), so this change's row is renumbered to 21 with its enum digest measured on the moved tree (d6fc2fcfa8a74a0c, Resources f013e36743d8d9e6 unchanged) and GLOBAL_RPC_REVISION 21, which `the_global_rpc_revision_matches_its_definitions` passes; the count pins are main's values plus the stack's tests (test.regular_crates 1960, both test.regular_crates_on_host entries 1946, test.hermit_unit 1320, test.hermit_unit_on_host 1314, test.detcore_unit and _on_host 3306, test.cli 769, test.cli_on_host 688). Pins (main's value plus this change's tests, each matching `cargo nextest list`): `test.cli` 751 → 769, `test.cli_on_host` 670 → 688, `test.detcore_unit` and `_on_host` 3269 → 3306, `test.hermit_unit` 1291 → 1320, `test.hermit_unit_on_host` 1285 → 1314, `test.regular_crates` 1934 → 1960, `test.regular_crates_on_host` 1920 → 1946. `ci/sync-cell-config.sh --check`, fmt and `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` are clean. Re-run at the new head (AMD host): `-p hermit-detcore --lib`: 3348 of 3348 passed; `-p hermit-run --lib` `watch_is_