`config::tests::legacy_backend_json_round_trips_every_backend_capabilities_constant` (stale capability expectations since main's Reverie `9443a6b28` pin, https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/issues/5012). The pins of `test.cli`, `test.cli_on_host`, `test.detcore_unit`, `test.detcore_unit_on_host`, `test.hermit_unit`, `test.hermit_unit_on_host` are main's value plus this change's tests; main `cd9e333e8` itself pins those cells below what they list (https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/issues/4998), so their counts differ from the listing by main's own amount. On a bare-metal Intel host, where `--strict` runs: `a_hit_that_resets_an_ignored_sigtrap_stops_the_run`, `a_thread_that_blocks_sigtrap_never_arms_and_the_trace_says_so`, `a_watch_survives_exec_into_an_image_that_stores_first`, `an_access_trace_leaves_a_replayed_run_unchanged`, `every_lit_fixture_is_a_case_or_waits_for_its_guest`, `every_lit_fixture_is_within_the_supported_subset`, `lit_timerfd_virtual_time_hermit_run_strict`, `watch_hits_name_both_writers_and_leave_the_run_unchanged` passed. Main has since moved to `5662f36a9`. Against it this head conflicts at one doc line in detcore-model/src/config.rs (`to_legacy_backend_json`'s capability paragraph), where main's 189f1ae1a adds a sentence on `provides_guest_backtraces` and this change adds one on `hardware_watchpoints`: keep both sentences, main's first. Everything else conflicts only at the count pins. Revision 6 was `fb39308d1`. Carry-over: both reviewers approved this change at `fb39308d1`; its own patch, apart from the count pins, is identical commit by commit, except for mechanical resolutions (RPC row renumbering, checked by the RPC digest test `the_global_rpc_revision_matches_its_definitions`; legacy-key list union, checked by detcore-model's legacy-form tests), and its tests pass at this head.\n\n**Revision 8:** rebased onto main `d192e5d72`, on #4739's new head `d9eada660` (Reverie pin unchanged). Code conflicts resolved: detcore-model/src/config.rs:3216 and :3231: main's 189f1ae1a and this change both edited the legacy-form doc comment. It keeps main's `provides_guest_backtraces` sentence and adds this change's \"`hardware_watchpoints` reads back as 0, DBT's\" on its own line, and the count of capabilities added after the legacy form froze is now twelve (each side had raised it from ten to eleven for its own capability). detcore/src/config.rs:182 and detcore/src/tool_global.rs:7625: main took global RPC revision 21, so this change's row becomes 22 with the digest `the_global_rpc_revision_matches_its_definitions` measures at this head (9cb330f2bca9c63f). Pins are main's values plus this change's tests. Pins (main's value plus this change's tests, each matching `cargo nextest list`): `test.cli` 769 → 782, `test.cli_on_host` 688 → 701, `test.detcore_unit` and `_on_host` 3306 → 3375, `test.hermit_unit` 1320 → 1330, `test.hermit_unit_on_host` 1314 → 1324, `test.regular_crates` 1960 → 1963, `test.regular_crates_on_host` 1946 → 1949. `ci/sync-cell-config.sh --check`, fmt and `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` are clean. Re-run at the new head (AMD host): `-p hermit-detcore --lib`: 3375 of 3375 passed; `-p hermit-run --lib` `watch_is_refused_where_it_could_not_arm_or_report`: 1 of 1 passed; `-p hermit-run --test cli` 4 named tests: 4 of 4 passed; `-p detcore-model --lib` `a_watch_takes_an_address_a_length_and_an_access`, `config_fingerprint_includes_the_watch_element_layout`: 2 of 2 passed; `-p hermit-run --test lit`: 96 of 98 passed, the same as main on this host (`lit_timerfd_virtual_time_hermit_run_strict` stops at the `--strict` refusal, exit 122, and `lit_scheduler_strategies_chaos_verify` times out at 57 s); `-p hermit-run --lib`: 465 of 472 passed; the other 7 fail the same way at main `d192e5d72` on this host: `ptrace_completion::tests::real_random_copy_failure_retires_initialized_sibling_and_timer`, `ptrace_completion::tests::real_random_copy_failure_with_trace_diagnostics`, `ptrace_completion::tests::real_random_live_copy_preserves_sibling_and_timer_success`, `ptrace_completion::tests::real_random_readv_import_failure_retires_initialized_sibling_and_timer`, `ptrace_completion::tests::real_random_readv_live_import_preserves_sibling_and_timer_success` (host stack-size and VM-counter limits); `tests::detcore_drives_kvm_guest_for_synthetic_syscall`, `tests::kvm_runs_dynamic_echo_through_detcore` (this VM's KVM guest clock); `-p detcore-model --lib`: 325 of 325 passed. On a bare-metal Intel host, where `--strict` runs: `a_hit_that_resets_an_ignored_sigtrap_stops_the_run`, `a_thread_that_blocks_sigtrap_never_arms_and_the_trace_says_so`, `a_watch_survives_exec_into_an_image_that_stores_first`, `an_access_trace_leaves_a_replayed_run_unchanged`, `every_lit_fixture_is_a_case_or_waits_for_its_guest`, `every_lit_fixture_is_within_the_supported_subset`, `lit_guest_held_polls_hermit_run`, `lit_scheduler_strategies_chaos_verify`, `lit_timerfd_virtual_time_hermit_run_strict`, `watch_hits_name_both_writers_and_leave_the_run_unchanged` passed. Main has since moved to `694f5df2f`; this head merges into it without a code conflict (count-pin files only, left to the lander). Revision 7 was `0733aed05`. Delta review: the reviewers review the interdiff from `0733aed05` (detcore-model/src/config.rs doc comment (main 189f1ae1a's sentence kept, this change's `hardware_watchpoints` line added, \"eleven\" -> \"twelve\")); the RPC row renumbering is mechanical.\n\n**Revision 9:** rebased onto main `fcd62385f` (Reverie pin unchanged, main's `940ac8d7e`); this change's own diff is unchanged. #4739 landed on main, so its seven commits drop out of this branch (all but one of their 2,177 added lines are on main verbatim; one documentation line was reworded at landing), and this PR is now its own four commits plus one rebase fix, directly on main. Resolutions, only where main moved: detcore-model/src/config.rs, the legacy-form documentation keeps main's `places_orphans`/`publishable_parent_death_signals` sentence beside this change's \"`hardware_watchpoints` reads back as 0, DBT's\", and the count of capabilities added after the legacy form froze is fourteen (main raised it to thirteen); the legacy-key list holds main's `sleep_registration` and `strict_binder` beside this change's `watch` and `watch_from` (50 entries, thirty-five keys fewer than fields). detcore-model/src/summary.rs and detcore/src/scheduler.rs, `RunSummary` holds main's `desync_notes` and `binder_external_calls` (their types and report line) beside `watch` and `WatchRunSummary`. hermit-cli/src/bin/hermit/run.rs, `--watch`'s refusal stays where it was and the DBT `--scheduler-turn-cost` check main removed with the core split stays removed (an external adapter is refused by main's access-trace check before `--watch` could reach the backend's watchpoint count); \"Rebase fix: follow main's crate::app module paths\" gives this change's refusal test main's `crate::app::Args`. Global RPC: main took revisions 22 to 24, so this change's row becomes 25, digest `972afd3cae07a4c4` measured by `the_global_rpc_revision_matches_its_definitions` at this head (Resources `f013e36743d8d9e6` unchanged); #4769, #4728, #4867 and #4791 also claim 25 on this base. RECORD_VERSION and the preemption record format are untouched. Count pins are main's values plus this change's tests.\n\nChecks at this head on an Intel Xeon Gold 6138 bare-metal host (ptrace backend, default log level, no relaxations; Reverie `940ac8d7e` from Cargo's git database, no `[patch]`): `cargo fmt --all -- --check` clean; `cargo clippy -p hermit-detcore -p hermit-run -p detcore-model -p hermit-verify --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean; `RUSTDOCFLAGS='-D warnings' cargo doc --no-deps -p hermit-detcore -p detcore-model -p hermit-run` passes; `scripts/check-doc-bare-urls.rs` passes; `cargo nextest run --cargo-profile validate -p hermit-detcore --lib`: 3471 run, 3471 passed; `cargo nextest run --cargo-profile validate -p detcore-model -p hermit-run --lib --bins`: 1506 run, 1506 passed, 1 skipped; this change's four CLI watch tests (`access_trace::watch_hits_name_both_writers_and_leave_the_run_unchanged`, `a_thread_that_blocks_sigtrap_never_arms_and_the_trace_says_so`, `a_hit_that_resets_an_ignored_sigtrap_stops_the_run`, `a_watch_survives_exec_into_an_image_that_stores_first`; `-p hermit-run --features liteinst --test cli`): 4 passed; `privileged-test.pmu_cli_cases`' 22 exact terms (`-p hermit-run --features liteinst --test cli -j 1`, under `--strict` with the PMU): 22 passed; `ci/sync-cell-config.sh --check` passes; count pins against `cargo nextest list` with each node's arguments: `test.regular_crates` 1953, `test.hermit_unit` 1222, `test.detcore_unit` and `_on_host` 3471, `test.regular_crates_on_host` 1939, `test.hermit_unit_on_host` 1216 match; `test.cli` 798 and `test.cli_on_host` 717 are main's 794 and 713 plus this change's four CLI tests (the listing helper reads 23 fewer than the pin for both on main `fcd62385f` too, 771 and 690, and 775 and 694 here, so the gap is the helper's, not this change's). The pinned-root image main now names (`7facbb1c`) is not loaded on that host, so these are host-level checks, not a pinned-root validation run.\n","headRefOid":"c5b4f7edfe861f7147f3253a116ecb46d4afaa11","state":"OPEN"}
